      "message": "Cherry pick is not clean. These are the differences between the original change and this cherry-pick:\nChecked against UPSTREAM commit: [googlesource](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/71479eee9da8ddb53f3ddb91bc8591d90fb8b142) [kernel.org](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003d71479eee9da8ddb53f3ddb91bc8591d90fb8b142)\n\n```\n      ## rust/Makefile ##\n     @@ rust/Makefile: quiet_cmd_rustdoc \u003d RUSTDOC $(if $(rustdoc_host),H, ) $\u003c\n    @@ rust/Makefile: quiet_cmd_rustdoc \u003d RUSTDOC $(if $(rustdoc_host),H, ) $\u003c\n      \t\t@$(objtree)/include/generated/rustc_cfg $\u003c\n      \n      # The `html_logo_url` and `html_favicon_url` forms of the `doc` attribute\n    -@@ rust/Makefile: quiet_cmd_rustdoc_test_kernel \u003d RUSTDOC TK $\u003c\n    - \t\t--extern build_error --extern macros \\\n    - \t\t--extern bindings --extern uapi \\\n    - \t\t--no-run --crate-name kernel -Zunstable-options \\\n    -+\t\t--sysroot\u003d/dev/null \\\n    - \t\t--test-builder $(objtree)/scripts/rustdoc_test_builder \\\n    - \t\t$\u003c $(rustdoc_test_kernel_quiet); \\\n    - \t$(objtree)/scripts/rustdoc_test_gen\n     @@ rust/Makefile: quiet_cmd_rustc_library \u003d $(if $(skip_clippy),RUSTC,$(RUSTC_OR_CLIPPY_QUIET)) L\n    + \t\t--emit\u003ddep-info\u003d$(depfile) --emit\u003dobj\u003d$@ \\\n      \t\t--emit\u003dmetadata\u003d$(dir $@)$(patsubst %.o,lib%.rmeta,$(notdir $@)) \\\n      \t\t--crate-type rlib -L$(objtree)/$(obj) \\\n    - \t\t--crate-name $(patsubst %.o,%,$(notdir $@)) $\u003c \\\n     +\t\t--sysroot\u003d/dev/null \\\n    + \t\t--crate-name $(patsubst %.o,%,$(notdir $@)) $\u003c; \\\n    + \tsed -i \u0027/^\\#/d\u0027 $(depfile) \\\n      \t$(if $(rustc_objcopy),;$(OBJCOPY) $(rustc_objcopy) $@)\n    - \n    - rust-analyzer:\n     \n      ## scripts/Makefile.build ##\n     @@ scripts/Makefile.build: rust_common_cmd \u003d \\\n    @@ scripts/Makefile.build: rust_common_cmd \u003d \\\n     +\t--sysroot\u003d/dev/null \\\n      \t--out-dir $(dir $@) --emit\u003ddep-info\u003d$(depfile)\n      \n    - # `--emit\u003dobj`, `--emit\u003dasm` and `--emit\u003dllvm-ir` imply a single codegen unit\n    + rust_handle_depfile \u003d \\\n```\n\nPlease refer to the contribution guidelines for details:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md",
